            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Treat the equation as a quadratic in ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "4^x",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", then use logarithms.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $u=4^x>0$. Since $16^x=(4^x)^2$ and $2^{2x+3}=8(4^x)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-8u+15&=0\\\\(u-3)(u-5)&=0\\\\u&=3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad u=5.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}4^x&=3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 4^x=5\\\\2x&=\\log_2 3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2x=\\log_2 5\\\\x&=\\frac12\\log_2 3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac12\\log_2 5.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
